  "Id": 154,
  "Title": "AKU faculty secures prestigious scholarship",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Boston Children\u2019s Hospital\u2019s Global Paediatric Innovation Summit+Awards 2015",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClass3377EDE474204DE7A50FE421D6C921E5\"><div>AKU\u2019s Dr Nadeem Aslam has been awarded an international scholarship to attend the Boston Children\u2019s Hospital\u2019s Global Paediatric Innovation Summit + Awards 2015, \u2018Taking on Tomorrow\u2019.</div><div><br></div><div>The scholarship supports a select number of clinicians, researchers or investors residing outside the U.S.A. with a confirmed interest in the advancement of paediatric innovation.</div><div><br></div><div>Dr Aslam, assistant professor and paediatric cardiologist in the Department of Paediatrics and Child Health, will be one of the delegates representing Asia at the Summit.</div><div><br></div><div>\u201cOn an almost daily basis, our resource limited setting provides a strong stimulus to innovate, to customize, to invent, to think out-of-the-box and to do things that are sometimes \u2018crazy\u2019 to help those who need it the most,\u201d says Dr Aslam. \u201cThis is&#160;what I feel, leads to innovation and to making this world a better place to live in.\u201d</div><div>At this year\u2019s Summit, Dr Aslam will have the opportunity to interact with the \u201cintelligent minds of the world\u201d and thought-provoking leaders, to ignite advances and accelerate solutions in paediatric health care, from the moment an idea is conceived to its entrance in the health care.</div><div><br></div><div>\u201cI am looking for long-term collaboration between the Boston Children\u2019s Hospital and the Aga Khan University,\u201d Dr Aslam emphasised, \u201ca partnership that can spark change in the way we treat our child patients.&quot;</div><div><br></div></div>",
